"""
Data integrity validation for profiling_results.json files.

Targets c2_qw_n500 (duplicate process risk) but works for any experiment.
Checks: problem count, index monotonicity, ID uniqueness, NaN/Inf values,
config consistency, cross-condition problem alignment.

Null ii_mid values are expected (problems with no mid-phase segments).
Null ii_high/ii_low is tolerated up to 10% — the analysis code skips them.
The critical checks are: duplicate problem_ids and wrong problem counts.

Usage:
    python validate_data_integrity.py                         # validate all
    python validate_data_integrity.py --pattern "n500*qw*"    # filter
    python validate_data_integrity.py --dir profiling_output_bf16_ds_imp_s015
